      "type": "FirstPrinciple",
      "label": "Denialism and Silence Enable Oppression",
      "text": "Silence is not neutrality — it favors whoever benefits from the status quo. Strong default: silence is presumed enabling until shown otherwise. Exception: strategic disengagement where continued presence causes net harm.",
