      "label": "Social Fragmentation Model",
      "text": "Three pillars of democracy: social capital, strong institutions, shared stories. Social media weakened all three: too-fast feedback loops, outrage amplification, mob justice without due process, state-actor disinformation. Madison's design inverted.",
      "notes": "COGNITIVE CASCADE (v1.9): Prior analysis traced political consequence only. Book model adds cognitive cascade: Strategic Ignorance → Architecture of Ignorance → Algorithmic Complacency → High-Fructose Feed → Cognitive Malnourishment → Anti-intellectualism → Absolutism → Conceit of Knowledge. Endpoint: loss of capacity to know what you don't know. Two distinct interventions: political (structural/regulatory) vs. cognitive (rebuild discriminating attention and tolerance of complexity). FR-6 (DFW: 'learning how to think') is the positive antidote at the cognitive level. See FR-19 (Negative Capability)."
    },
