      "text": "~17,000 participants through Kaiser Permanente. Dose-response relationship: higher ACE score directly predicts adult chronic disease (heart disease, cancer, liver disease), mental health disorders, and shortened lifespan. Mechanism is physiological: chronic stress dysregulates HPA axis, producing lasting biological changes. Institutional non-adoption of ACE screening (most physicians untrained; not integrated into standard protocols) is itself evidence of the harm-avoidance frame in operation — costs of screening (time, scope uncertainty) are immediate; costs of inaction (missed root causes, downstream disease) are deferred and diffuse. Anchors FP-16, FR-22, DB-24.",
